<title>USA: Fed adds reserves via overnight system RPs Tuesday.</title>
<headline>Fed adds reserves via overnight system RPs Tuesday.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve added reserves to the banking system via a round of overnight system repurchase agreements Tuesday, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York confirmed.</p>
<p>The operation had been expected by economists, who also said the Fed could permanently inject funds into the system via another coupon &quot;pass,&quot; or outright purchase of securities, at any time.</p>
<p>(( -- J. Hughes, N.A. Treasury desk, 212-859-1663))</p>
